 "old": {
  "example": "<b>What it costs here at 2027 rates (USDA files read Nov 4, 2026):</b> you pay $444 a year, $4.44 an acre, for 100 acres of grazing at 90% coverage, productivity factor 100, half in April to May and half in June to July, on grid 25342, the middle of the county&rsquo;s 9 grids by premium. USDA pays $461 of the $905 full premium. Run over 1951 to 2025 at 2027 rates, it would have paid in 51 of 75 years, an average of $792 a year, or $7.92 an acre. That average is under the full premium of $905; it comes out above your share only because USDA pays the rest. That is the past record, not a forecast, and it leaves out the administrative fee. Example, not a recommendation.",
